            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for to tease, then the Bengali for to tickle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: গম্ভীর",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গম্ভীর — gômbhīr — \"grave; serious\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "খবরটা শুনে বাবা গম্ভীর হয়ে গেলেন। khôbôrṭā shune bābā gômbhīr hôye gelen. Father went grave when he heard the news."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "গম্ভীর (gômbhīr) is a tatsama, Sanskrit gambhīra, \"deep\" (CDIAL 4031), which Monier-Williams gives as a form of gabhīra, the source of গভীর (taught), deep; Bengali uses it for a deep, serious manner."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
